HI</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>NOGUCHI, YASUHIKO</last-name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>KAKISAKA YOUICHI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>KUWAHARA KOICHI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>NOGUCHI YASUHIKO</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>KAKISAKA, YOUICHI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>KUWAHARA, KOICHI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>NOGUCHI, YASUHIKO</last-name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A robot off-line teaching method for determining the last position and the last posture of a robot (2) when the robot (2) capable of stopping at an arbitrary location on a traveling axis (1) and taking an arbitrary position at the arbitrary location starts from an arbitrary initial location while taking an initial posture and moves while changing the position and posture so that its control point (5) moves to a movement target (7). The last position is determined on the traveling axis (1) of the robot (2) in such a way that the distance between the coordinate origin (3) of the robot (2) and the movement target point (7) is the shortest.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un procédé d'apprentissage hors ligne d'un robot (2) permettant d'en déterminer la dernière position et la dernière posture. Ledit robot, capable de s'arrêter en un point arbitraire d'un axe de translation (1) et de prendre une posture arbitraire audit point arbitraire, part d'une position initiale dans une posture initiale, puis change de position et de posture de manière à ce que son point de commande (5) s'oriente vers une cible (7) en mouvement. La dernière position est déterminée sur l'axe de translation (1) du robot (2) de manière à ce que la distance entre l'origine (3) des coordonnées du robot (2) et le point (7) de la cible en mouvement soit la plus courte.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>